# Custody and physical holding establish protection duties, not shelter or speech actuality.
# ── Chapter 27 fidelity pins: "The One Thing Taken" ──────────────────────────
#
# Custodial safeguards and release duties do not create a second deprivation:
#   tests/pins/justice/conditions/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/release-review/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/continuity/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/boundaries/no-person-consequences-or-forged-orders/expect.pins.nibli
# None supplies physical release, observed conditions or an arrival receipt.
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/27-the-one-thing-taken.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the other substantive cases and contradiction scans
#
# Release: a raw report that a sentence is finished makes a person of the name
# it gives, through the `free -> person` rule, and ends no custody; a
# qualified custody-relief order in the case ends it. The release section
# below pins both.
#
# Duration is an external supplied boundary, not a counted sentence; the
# time-vocabulary refusals below are substantive checks.
#
# "movement and a recorded loss are endpoints, which the rules conclude and
# read nowhere": `travel` and `lose` appear in the constitution only as rule
# heads. Test the rule BODIES, since a bare grep matches the head too:
#   awk -F'->' '/^[^#]/ && /->/ && $1 ~ /travel/' book-1/source/constitution.nibli
# must stay EMPTY. The `:require` lines below run this check for both
# relations, with a positive control.

# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE — three kinds, and only one is a verdict. A FALSE on a
# corpus name this KB never mentions is real but empty: nothing could have made
# it TRUE. A non-corpus name is not a FALSE at all — the run aborts, pins not
# trustworthy. And a well-formed query on an argument its relation never
# carries is a vacuous green that passes forever. Article 0a closes the
# ASSERTION side only — a widening fact aborts the run rather than loading —
# but a QUERY on an unmentioned name still answers a clean FALSE, so kind one
# is untouched. Pin a FALSE only where the KB could have said TRUE, and say in
# the comment what would flip it.

:expect-pins 47

# The order may be read; the loss and free-movement capability may not.
# This checks the enacted source with a live positive control. The authoring
# development test separately inspects the compiled dependency graph.
:require test -z "$(awk -F'->' '/^[^#]/ && /->/ && $1 ~ /(^|[^[:alnum:]_])(travel|lose)[[:space:]]*\(/ {print}' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)"
:require test -n "$(awk -F'->' '/^[^#]/ && /->/ && $1 ~ /(^|[^[:alnum:]_])restrain[[:space:]]*\(/ {print}' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)"

# "Custody follows, and with it the loss of movement."
? prisoner(Hano).
# => TRUE

? travel(Hano).
# => FALSE

# "Hano remains a person, owed the whole floor, with a ballot entitlement."
# Item by item; no credibility finding or recorded loss follows either.
? person(Hano).
# => TRUE

# Custody leaves Hano the claims, not the things claimed: the record "contains
# no shelter receipt or record of speech", so the rules conclude no speech.
? expresses(Hano).
# => FALSE

? decide(Hano, Ballot).
# => TRUE

? false(Hano).
# => FALSE

? lose(Points, Hano).
# => FALSE

# Nor shelter received: a reviewed home placement is no shelter receipt.
? dwell(Hano).
# => FALSE

# Hano and Jala share an injury entry, not a complete record of culpability.
? injure(Jala, Ivo).
# => TRUE

? prisoner(Jala).
# => FALSE

? travel(Jala).
# => TRUE

# A credibility finding is not confinement: Bela is under one and still moves.
? false(Bela).
# => TRUE

? travel(Bela).
# => TRUE

# ── "What leaving changes" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This block records a release for Hano, and the record keeps it for the rest
# of the file: later queries about Hano, including the custody-authority pin
# in the time block, see the released Hano.

# "Suppose entries were added to end Hano's custody." The first is a raw report
# that the sentence is finished.
free(Hano).

# A raw completion report has no authority; the qualified case order does.
? prisoner(Hano).
# => TRUE
? travel(Hano).
# => FALSE
# The qualified order follows: Appeals, with an independent reviewer, finds
# the sentence satisfied. It "identifies Hano, the case, incident, offence,
# ground, evidence and appellate actors"; witnesses fix its place in sequence.
list(Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Hano, Case_Hano, CustodyRelief).
list(Chapter29_Hano_Completion, SentenceSatisfied, Evidence_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, CustodyReliefGroundEvidence).
judge(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion).
judge(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion).
authorized(Appeals, CustodyAppellateAuthority, Chapter29_Hano_Completion).
authorized(CustodyAppealReview, IndependentCustodyDispositionReviewer, Chapter29_Hano_Completion).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Hano, CustodyReliefSubjectScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Hano, CustodyReliefSubjectScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Case_Hano, CustodyReliefCaseScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Case_Hano, CustodyReliefCaseScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Incident_Case_Hano, CustodyReliefIncidentScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Incident_Case_Hano, CustodyReliefIncidentScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, PublicInjuryOffence, CustodyReliefOffenceScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, PublicInjuryOffence, CustodyReliefOffenceScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, SentenceSatisfied, CustodyReliefGroundScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, SentenceSatisfied, CustodyReliefGroundScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Evidence_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, CustodyReliefEvidenceScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Evidence_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, CustodyReliefEvidenceScope).
observe(Appeals, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, NoticeCounselEvidenceAccessHearingAndReasons, CustodyReliefProcedureScope).
observe(CustodyAppealReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, NoticeCounselEvidenceAccessHearingAndReasons, CustodyReliefProcedureScope).
observe(Chronicle, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Appeals, CustodyAppealActorEligibleAtDecisionScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Appeals, CustodyAppealActorEligibleAtDecisionScope).
observe(Chronicle, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, CustodyAppealReview, CustodyDispositionReviewerEligibleAtDecisionScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, CustodyAppealReview, CustodyDispositionReviewerEligibleAtDecisionScope).
list(Relief_Start_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Case_Hano, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, RecordSequence).
observe(Chronicle, Relief_Start_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Case_Hano, RecordStartScope).
observe(Chronicle, Relief_Start_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, RecordEndScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Relief_Start_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Case_Hano, RecordStartScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Relief_Start_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, RecordEndScope).
list(Relief_End_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Epoch_Current, RecordSequence).
observe(Chronicle, Relief_End_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, RecordStartScope).
observe(Chronicle, Relief_End_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Epoch_Current, RecordEndScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Relief_End_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Chapter29_Hano_Completion, RecordStartScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Relief_End_Chapter29_Hano_Completion, Epoch_Current, RecordEndScope).

# Release changes the custody, movement and marker conclusions; it does not
# establish physical release.
? prisoner(Hano).
# => FALSE

? travel(Hano).
# => TRUE

? err(Hano, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# "Hano keeps standing and is still owed shelter": personhood, the shelter
# entitlement and the State's floor debt all hold after release.
? person(Hano).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Hano, event { dwell() }).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Provision, Hano).
# => TRUE

# "Shelter received, or speech made, needs evidence of its own, independent of
# the sentence and of the order ending it": neither follows for Hano after
# release, as neither followed during custody.
? expresses(Hano).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Hano).
# => FALSE

# ── Jala, item by item ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Jala holds only the injury entry: no speech or shelter is shown, no
# placement eligibility follows and no isolation marker is raised.
? expresses(Jala).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Jala).
# => FALSE

? fit(Jala, Homestay).
# => FALSE

? err(Jala, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# and Jala is genuinely unconvicted — the control for all four
? prisoner(Jala).
# => FALSE

# ── "The review period has an order, and no length the rules measure." ─────
# The design does not say how long. Time words are refused at assertion, and
# a visible `admits` line (chapter 2's closure) is the only way in. The record
# holds an independently witnessed transition, separately witnessed orders of
# events and of record entries, and a reviewed custody interval: symbolic
# record relations, not a clock or a computed term.
? succeed(Epoch_Current, Transition).
# => TRUE

? precede(Order_Court_A, EventSequence).
# => TRUE

? precede(Order_Log_Court_A, RecordSequence).
# => TRUE

? time(Window_Custody, ReviewedInterval).
# => TRUE

# The witnessed relations stay, but the qualified order above ends custody in
# Hano's case: the rules conclude no ActivePower for Case_Hano.
? correct(Case_Hano, ActivePower).
# => FALSE

# `year` and `earlier` remain unadmitted negative controls. Their refusal does
# not prove the model has no temporal path; it proves date-shaped words cannot
# bypass the reviewed path through the loud vocabulary door.
:refuse reasoning /not admitted vocabulary/
year(Term, Two).

:refuse reasoning /not admitted vocabulary/
earlier(Custody, Release).

# ── "Recognition, employment, compliance, wealth and character are outside the
# terms on which custody continues or ends" ──────────────────────────────────
# Recognition has no producer or reader. A proposed raw release rule loads,
# but its premise has no source and a raw release flag grants no authority.
# The operative rule below still defeats its own custody premise.
:accept-scoped
all $x: prisoner($x) & reward($x) -> free($x).
# An attempted operative recognition-based release has the negative cycle.
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable/
all $subject: all $case: prisoner($subject, $case) & reward($subject) -> clean($case, CustodyConfinementBar).

# ── THE TERM THAT RELEASES NOBODY ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# "Suppose a duration word were admitted and a term recorded for a person still
# held. Custody continues and the rules conclude no release." Here it is done:
# admit the word, state the term — no digit anywhere, `Two` is an opaque name.
# Ruk is the subject because this file has already released Hano above.
# "A term label by itself is only a label, with nothing to count it down or
# bring it to an end." The entries stay in the record for the rest of the
# file; no rule reads `year`, so the child block below is unaffected.
#
# `admits` for a FRESH name loads from a probe (the too-late refusal guards
# relations with prior facts), so this ceremony can be performed on top of
# the record from outside the constitution's text.
# In the society, the widening is still the visible reviewable act chapter 2
# describes; in this harness, it means refusal pins guard the shipped text and
# a probe may always widen on top — which is exactly what this block does.
admits("year").
year(Term_Ruk, Two).

? prisoner(Ruk).
# => TRUE

? free(Ruk).
# => FALSE

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On the one-line birth record, Nell moves freely, and no restraint or
# confinement follows.
? travel(Nell).
# => TRUE

? restrain(Nell).
# => FALSE

? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE

# For the child fixture the rules conclude neither a credibility finding nor
# a recorded loss, and the food debt remains.
? false(Nell).
# => FALSE

? lose(Points, Nell).
# => FALSE

? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE
